---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EMAIL, LINKS, LOCATION } from '../consts';
import { url } from '../lib/posts';
import { projects } from '../data/work';
---

<Base title="About" ogImage="/og/about.png" description="Who I am and how I work.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I’m Habiba Faisal, a software engineer from {LOCATION}. I’ve spent about three years in startups,
      mostly working directly with founders, across frontend, backend, mobile and product.
    </p>
    <p>
      There’s a pattern to my work. I join a company in a domain I don’t know and learn it well
      enough to build the central system. At Sail Wellness that was health and toxicology. At
      Livedin it was property management in Saudi Arabia. At a stealth US freight-factoring startup it was invoice finance,
      where I built the funding-decision engine, the ledger and money movement.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      What I’m good at is translation between the product, the domain
      and the code. If I understand the business and the operator’s day well enough, a small change
      can have an outsized effect.
    </p>
    <p>
      I like staying close to operations and the business. When someone asks for a feature, I look
      for the real pain behind it: in reviews, in engagement, and in the things that don’t show up in
      metrics. Then I fix it, and check whether the fix worked.
    </p>
    <p>
      I care about detail, and Apple is a big influence there. Soon after I joined Sail, the app felt
      wrong, even though it matched the design file. I traced it to the font. Changing it changed the
      whole app.
    </p>

    <h2>Earlier</h2>
    <p>
      I studied computer science at SZABIST in Karachi and graduated as the silver medalist. Right
      after, I taught there for a semester as adjunct faculty: Software Development and Construction.
      Explaining things to a room is still how I check whether I understand them.
    </p>
    <p>
      I was once acknowledged by the US Department of Defense for a responsible vulnerability
      disclosure.
    </p>

    <h2>Side projects</h2>
    {
      projects.map((p) => (
        <p>
          <a href={p.href}>{p.name}</a>. {p.body}
        </p>
      ))
    }

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      The best way to reach me is email: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. My
      <a href={url('/habiba-faisal-resume.pdf')}>résumé</a> is a one-page PDF. I’m also on
      {LINKS.map((l, i) => (<>{i > 0 && (i === LINKS.length - 1 ? ' and ' : ', ')}<a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a></>))}.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
